<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Katsina Emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">1807 CE – 1903 CE · capital Katsina</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The emirate that replaced the Hausa kingdom of Katsina after the jihad, ruled by Fulani emirs while the old dynasty carried on at Maradi.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1807 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> scholar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umaru-dallaji">Umaru Dallaji</a>, a follower of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a>, captured <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/katsina-kingdom">Katsina</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> ruler, who fled north and eventually founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-maradi">Sultanate of Maradi</a>. Dallaji became the first emir and founded the dynasty that ruled until the colonial period.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/katsina-kingdom">Katsina</a> had been the leading commercial and scholarly city of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hausa-kingdoms">Hausaland</a>, but war with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-maradi">Maradi</a> and the rise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a> drew trade away during the 19th century. The emir governed with titled officials, many offices inherited from the Katsina Kingdom, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> remained a frontier power, constantly raided by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> exiles to the north. Islamic scholarship continued in its mosques and schools.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>British forces occupied <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/katsina-kingdom">Katsina</a> in 1903. In 1906 the British deposed the emir and appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammadu-dikko">Muhammadu Dikko</a>, founder of the Sullubawa dynasty, which still reigns. The northern part of the old kingdom lies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/katsina-emirate.jpg" alt="Katsina Emirate" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Hosmich · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Hausa_people.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1807 CE – 1903 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Katsina</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Umaru Dallaji, Muhammadu Dikko</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hausa, Fulfulde</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/nigeria">Nigeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Emirate of Katsina</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1855&amp;focus=katsina-emirate" aria-label="Katsina Emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4889 1694 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Katsina Emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5209 1950L5209 1950M5209 1950L5144 1947M5209 1950L5170 2068"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5209 1950h0M5144 1947h0M5170 2068h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5209 1950h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5209 1950h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Katsina. <a href="/atlas?year=1855&amp;focus=katsina-emirate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
